{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id43191505"}, "name":{"label":"Ross_b2"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2012-07-25T14:10:38-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.8.3"}, "id":{"label":"629112029"}, "title":{"label":"the best reminder app I have used"}, "content":{"label":"I have tried two other reminder apps, abandoning them due to lack of success. This one stands out, due to \n-excellent interface design, very quick to create new reminders, or amend existing ones\n-icons allow easy task amendment without editing, if you want to snooze for a short time, or an hour.\n-the custom notification sound is excellent\n-notifications every minute by default mean that nothing gets left until acknowledged.\n-there are extra animations and sound effects when doing tasks, which make the app feel polished and special. I wish every app had this level of animation and sound.\n\nThe app is relatively expensive, but definitely worth it.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=390017969&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"1"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"1"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id13000470"}, "name":{"label":"Lambo1982"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2012-06-17T12:12:17-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"5"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.8.3"}, "id":{"label":"603936991"}, "title":{"label":"Great App for the lazy and unorganized"}, "content":{"label":"The reminders are so annoying unless you do something about it. That suits me fine cause I can be sooo lazy to even do the simple of tasks!\n\nGreat app!", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=390017969&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id85909337"}, "name":{"label":"Matt_lucas"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2012-06-01T10:27:06-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"4"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.8.3"}, "id":{"label":"594035659"}, "title":{"label":"Great, but a couple of crucial limitations"}, "content":{"label":"This is a great app - I've just bought it for both iOS and Mac OS, and it synchronises and does everything it's supposed to. The crucial flaw as I see it at this stage is that the iOS version only synchronises (I'm using Dropbox as the sync method - I've no idea if it behaves the same using iCloud as the sync method) when you open and close the app. \n\nAll the reminders work fine when the app isn't working - I get all the notifications and everything. But if I mark a reminder as complete on my Mac, that isn't synchronised with the iOS version until I open it. That's the crucial flaw. The whole purpose of a seamless reminders app (which this is in virtually every other respect) is that you don't have to put effort into doing it - it should do it for you. Devs, please please fix it so that it updates live in the background, so I never need to actually open the app on my iDevice except to create new reminders or mark old ones as done. If I have to remember to open it to make sure my reminders are up to date - what's the point?\n\nThe only other complaint I have is the default 'snooze' times in iOS - 1 minute or 1 hour is very limited compared to the broad range of times available in Mac OS. However, I know the devs are aware of this one and are working on it, so it's a 'for now' complaint only. \n\nOther than that, it's brilliant - I love the \"do x tomorrow\" and it'll mark it for 9am, or \"do it in one hour\" or \"do it at 4\". Lovely, very refreshing and simple and quick. The only other thing I would suggest is have voice-recognition - how much easier would it be to have all those features but just SAY to your iPhone \"wake me up tomorrow at 6am\" or something like that. Perhaps Apple will allow Siri integration in iOS 6… who knows?\n\nGreat app all in all - needs a bit more to make it all that it could be though.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=390017969&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"0"}}, 
{"author":{"uri":{"label":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/reviews/id102328635"}, "name":{"label":"Sonny Manou"}, "label":""}, "updated":{"label":"2012-05-30T01:07:33-07:00"}, "im:rating":{"label":"1"}, "im:version":{"label":"1.8.3"}, "id":{"label":"592607207"}, "title":{"label":"Essential features modifications required."}, "content":{"label":"Don't get me wrong, this is a great program, but it needs a couple of features to be modified.\n\nOver a year ago, I personally contacted the developer about this. He said that he would modify the features for the next build. The mods didn't materialise, hence this poor review.\n\nI will rewrite this review when my requests have materialised.\n\nThe modified features requested were - and are: the requests are still needed.\n\n1. The repeated reminder alarm feature for the reminders feature needs to have more variable time limits. It is not up to the job: the time period options are either too long, or too short.\n\nAlong with the repeat options of 1 minute and 1 hour, the following default options are required:\n\n1. 5 mins\n2. 10 mins\n3. 20 mins\n4. 30 mins\n5. 45 mins\n\nThe other modification urgently required is more time allowed to quickly change the default snooze if needed.\n\nI would like to see the automatic hiding function removed from the additional options for the reminder being modified.\n\nThere is no need to hide it automatically AND it's very annoying whilst modifying a current alarm to have it beeping away at you AND disappearing whist you are trying to get in with it.\n\nThis review is solely to spur the developer to fix these issues. This is otherwise a good program - it just needs some attention.", "attributes":{"type":"text"}}, "link":{"attributes":{"rel":"related", "href":"https://itunes.apple.com/gb/review?id=390017969&type=Purple%20Software"}}, "im:voteSum":{"label":"0"}, "im:contentType":{"attributes":{"term":"Application", "label":"Application"}}, "im:voteCount":{"label":"3"}}, 
